From e79e1e96895182b4aae1652625d3250c23db1d8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:58:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Explain the bohr units in Psi4's trajectory xyz file

print_trajectory_xyz_file writes coordinates in bohr, and .xyz carries no
units field, so Avogadro reads them as angstroms and the structure comes
out 1.89x too large. Notes that the input side needs no change --
psi4.geometry() already defaults to angstroms -- and gives two fixes:
use history_to_xyz, which converts, or rescale the emitted file with a
new rescale_xyz helper. Adds a bond-length table for identifying which
units a trajectory is in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018EXyt7n8dX4k5dhdMU41um
---
 .../1h_geometry_optimization_animate.ipynb    | 115 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 115 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/1h_geometry_optimization_animate.ipynb b/resources/1h_geometry_optimization_animate.ipynb
index ab284c5..c0f79c6 100644
--- a/resources/1h_geometry_optimization_animate.ipynb
+++ b/resources/1h_geometry_optimization_animate.ipynb
@@ -237,6 +237,121 @@
     "    psi4.set_options({\"print_trajectory_xyz_file\": False})"
    ]
   },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Units: the input is already angstroms, the trajectory file is not\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Two separate questions, and only one of them is a problem.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Input side \u2014 nothing to fix.**  `psi4.geometry()` reads Cartesians in\n",
+    "**angstroms by default**, so coordinates pasted into the input string are already\n",
+    "interpreted the way you want.  (You would have to write `units bohr` *inside* the\n",
+    "geometry block to get anything else.)  If you want it stated explicitly rather than\n",
+    "relying on the default, add a `units angstrom` line:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "```python\n",
+    "mol = psi4.geometry(\"\"\"\n",
+    "0 1\n",
+    "units angstrom\n",
+    "C   -1.061709204   1.297140572   0.292060003\n",
+    "...\n",
+    "\"\"\")\n",
+    "```\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Output side \u2014 this is the one biting you.**  The file written by\n",
+    "`print_trajectory_xyz_file` is in **bohr**, and `.xyz` has no units field, so\n",
+    "Avogadro reads those numbers as angstroms and every atom lands 1.89x too far out.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Quick way to confirm which file you are looking at \u2014 check one bond against the\n",
+    "input geometry:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "| bond | correct (angstrom) | what you see if the file is bohr |\n",
+    "|---|---|---|\n",
+    "| C1=O2 | 1.225 | 2.314 |\n",
+    "| C1-O3 | 1.323 | 2.501 |\n",
+    "| O3-H4 | 0.994 | 1.879 |\n",
+    "| C1-C5 | 1.497 | 2.830 |\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**The one-line fix: don't use that file.**  `history_to_xyz` above already does the\n",
+    "bohr -> angstrom conversion, and you are already capturing `history`, so just call\n",
+    "it and drop the option:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "```python\n",
+    "psi4.set_options({\"print_trajectory_xyz_file\": False})   # or delete the line\n",
+    "...\n",
+    "history_to_xyz(mol, history, \"acoh_opt_traj.xyz\")        # writes angstroms\n",
+    "```\n",
+    "\n",
+    "If you would rather keep Psi4's own trajectory file, rescale it afterwards:"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "BOHR2ANG = 0.52917720859\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "def rescale_xyz(src, dest, factor=BOHR2ANG):\n",
+    "    \"\"\"Rescale every coordinate in a (possibly multi-frame) .xyz file.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "    factor=BOHR2ANG converts a bohr-unit trajectory -- what Psi4's\n",
+    "    print_trajectory_xyz_file emits -- into the angstroms Avogadro assumes.\n",
+    "    \"\"\"\n",
+    "    with open(src) as fh:\n",
+    "        lines = fh.read().split(\"\\n\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "    out, i, nframes = [], 0, 0\n",
+    "    while i < len(lines):\n",
+    "        if not lines[i].strip():              # tolerate blank padding between frames\n",
+    "            i += 1\n",
+    "            continue\n",
+    "        natom = int(lines[i].split()[0])      # atom-count line\n",
+    "        out.append(f\"{natom}\")\n",
+    "        out.append(lines[i + 1].rstrip())     # comment line, passed through\n",
+    "        for k in range(natom):\n",
+    "            parts = lines[i + 2 + k].split()\n",
+    "            s, xyz = parts[0], [float(v) * factor for v in parts[1:4]]\n",
+    "            out.append(f\"{s:<4s}{xyz[0]:>18.10f}{xyz[1]:>18.10f}{xyz[2]:>18.10f}\")\n",
+    "        nframes += 1\n",
+    "        i += 2 + natom\n",
+    "\n",
+    "    with open(dest, \"w\") as fh:\n",
+    "        fh.write(\"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\")\n",
+    "    return nframes\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "# nframes = rescale_xyz(\"acoh_opt.default.xyz\", \"acoh_opt_angstrom.xyz\")\n",
+    "# print(f\"rescaled {nframes} frames\")"
+   ],
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "outputs": []
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Sanity check either way: measure a bond in the first frame and compare it to the\n",
+    "input geometry.  If they agree, the units are right; if the ratio is 1.89, they are\n",
+    "not.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "```python\n",
+    "import numpy as np\n",
+    "xyz = open(\"acoh_opt_traj.xyz\").read().split(\"\\n\")\n",
+    "c = np.array([float(v) for v in xyz[2].split()[1:4]])   # C1\n",
+    "o = np.array([float(v) for v in xyz[3].split()[1:4]])   # O2\n",
+    "print(f\"C=O in frame 0: {np.linalg.norm(c - o):.4f} A   (input: 1.2247 A)\")\n",
+    "```\n",
+    "\n",
+    "One thing to carry over from Route A into your acetic acid script: it is still\n",
+    "missing `fix_com(True)` and `fix_orientation(True)`.  Without them Psi4 re-centers\n",
+    "and re-orients at every step, so the animation shows the molecule tumbling rather\n",
+    "than the C-O bonds relaxing \u2014 which is a much more confusing artifact than wrong\n",
+    "units, because the structure still *looks* chemically reasonable in each frame."
+   ]
+  },
   {
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "metadata": {},
-- 
